  "result": "Perfect! All 91 tests pass. I've successfully implemented line discounts across the invoicing system:\n\n**Added to `src/errors.js`:**\n- DISCOUNT_INVALID error code\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n- `createInvoice` now accepts `discountPercent` on each line (0-100, can have decimals)\n  - Defaults to 0 if not provided\n  - Validates: must be a number between 0-100, returns DISCOUNT_INVALID otherwise\n- New `lineDiscount(line)` function calculates line discount using precision rounding\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, total }`\n  - `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n  - `total` = subtotal - discount (clamped at 0)\n- Updated `addLine()` to accept and validate `discountPercent`\n\n**Updated `src/render.js`:**\n- Shows per-line discounts indented below each line when present\n- Shows total discount summary line when there are discounts\n- All amounts formatted through `formatEuros()`\n\n**Key design decisions implemented:**\n- All amounts can never go below zero\u2014clamped at 0\n- Discount calculations use `roundCents()` for precision\n- Line discount = lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100\n- Decimal percentages fully supported (e.g., 12.5%)\n\n**Tests added (21 new tests):**\n- Discount input validation and defaults\n- Decimal discount acceptance\n- lineDiscount calculation with proper rounding\n- invoiceTotals with discounts\n- Clamping behavior\n- addLine discount validation\n- Rendering discounts in text output\n\nAll 91 tests pass. Ready for the next request!",
